# Build-context exclusions for docker/console.Dockerfile ONLY.
#
# BuildKit prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over a context-root
# `.dockerignore`, which is why this file is named after the Dockerfile instead
# of sitting at the repository root: the console build is the only build in this
# tree whose context contains a Node toolchain, and a root-level ignore file
# would silently change what `docker/sdk-harness.Dockerfile` and
# `examples/fraud_triage_dataflow/Dockerfile` see.
#
# Without this, `frontend/node_modules/` (~180 packages) and the locally built
# `src/beam_agents/console/static/` bundle are uploaded to the daemon on every
# build — and the second one is actively wrong: the image must serve the bundle
# the pinned Node stage produced, never whatever a developer last built by hand.

# Node toolchain output. `npm ci` runs inside the frontend stage.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/screenshots/
frontend/*.tsbuildinfo

# A host-built UI bundle. The image's bundle comes from the frontend stage.
src/beam_agents/console/static/

# Python and tooling caches — never valid inputs to an image build.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
mutants/
.mutmut-cache

# Repository material the console image never runs: docs, benchmarks, the spec
# tree, git history, and the e2e gate's spool.
.git/
.github/
site/
docs/
benchmarks/
openspec/
tests/
bench-results/
docker/e2e-spool/
.claude/
